ensus-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+04:16/60:00 c30/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_awppft0l","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/census-window.log"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[ERR][2026-09-16 21:18:04] Cycle 1 failed in 509s (exit 255)\n[INF][2026-09-16 21:18:06] --- Cycle 1/1 ---\n  2026-09-17T00:18:07Z\n--- aggregate: runs=0 timeouts=0 exit1=0\n--- aggregate: runs=10 timeouts=0 exit1=6\n--- aggregate: runs=12 timeouts=0 exit1=1\n--- requests in window: 0 (log rotated past window or clean window)\n--- runs (start UTC | timeout? turns tools exit fate):\n== census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-15 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n== census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-16 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n== census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-18 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\nSep 15 00:31:35 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=21, exit=0 \nSep 15 00:48:04 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=27, exit=0 \nSep 15 01:18:43 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=27, exit=1 \nSep 15 02:08:34 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=27, exit=0 \nSep 15 03:14:51 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=37, exit=0 \nSep 15 03:50:07 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=38, exit=0 \nSep 15 04:20:15 | to=0 | turns=2, tools=28, exit=0 \n