ensus-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+00:58/60:00 c14/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_07fc55x9","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/continuo_known_hosts root@10.66.0.5 'bash -s' < /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh continuo 2026-09-22"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[14:54:52] Command exited with code 2.\nOutput:\ncensus-window: REFUSED -- DAY=continuo is in the future (today=2026-09-22).\n  A future day has no journald lines by construction; recording its\n  empty verdict as a clean window manufactures a fake-clean record\n  (c358: continuo recorded two 2026-09-16 clean lines on 09-15).\n\n[t+01:02/60:00 c15/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_vr0hete4","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/continuo_known_hosts root@10.66.0.5 'bash -s' < /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh 2026-09-21 continuo"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[14:54:59] == census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-21 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n--- runs (start UTC | timeout? turns tools exit fate):\nSep 21 03:12:11 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=76